<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins Electrabel order.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins Electrabel order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engineering joint venture GEC Alsthom said on Monday it won an order from Electrabel of Belgium for a 350 MW combined cycle power plant worth more than 146 million ecu.</p>
<p>The turnkey project will be located at Baudour, near Mons, and follows a Tractebel tender.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a joint venture between General Electric Co Plc of Britain and Alcatel Alsthom.  </p>
<p>The power plant will incorprate a 226 MW 9FA gas turbine, together with a steam turbine, generator and boiler. The equipment will be made in Belgium, France and Britain. Electrical equipment will be supplied by Cegelec, an Alcatel Alsthom subsidiary, GEC Alsthom said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant is due to be commissioned in January 1999 and will be operated by Electrabel.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
